-- title:
--   Rational places over s meet a node ring or a disc
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $\kappa$ the residue field of the valuation subring $A$, and $F$ the field `fieldBar q M'`, which is `laurentBaseChange` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the level-$(q^2M',H)$ function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   **Standing data.** A prime $q$ with $5\le q$; a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ for which $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`, i.e. `A.LiesOverPrime q`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC κ` and its $M'$-th expansion `jqNModC κ M'`, whose members are by `hW` exactly the supersingular places, namely those $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` lies in `ssJSet q κ`; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-field generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`) into $F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective residue homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with push-forward of divisors, together with the compatibilities that constants of $A$ reduce to their $\kappa$-residues and that every nonzero element can be scaled by a constant into the integers with nonzero residue; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a chosen element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   **Base layer.** A subfield $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`), such that $A_0:=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian local (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); the hypothesis `hκ` that every $a\in A$ can be written as $c$ plus an element of the maximal ideal of $A$, for some $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$. Auxiliary data: a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ that is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`). Finally, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$ (`hKb`), a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements of $K_b$ lying in $A$ (`hAb`), and a generator $\varpi_b\ne0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`).
--
--   The conclusion is a statement about all further data of the following kinds, $F$ being regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\hookrightarrow\bar{\mathbb Q}\to F$.
--
--   **The descended model.** An intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ subject to: (K1) the constants $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ generate $F$, i.e. `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F)) ⊔ F₀ = ⊤`; the agreement $x\in A\iff$ the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, for $x\in k_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; and (LD) the linear disjointness statement that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar{\mathbb Q}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to F$ with all $a_i$ in `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀` (image of $K'$) $\sqcup\,F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   **The affine chart.** A subring $B$ of $F$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure `alg` such that: the structure map sends $a\in A_b$ to its image in $F$ under $K_b\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}\to F$; $B$ is contained in `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀` (image of $K_b$) $\sqcup\,F_0$ and every element of that field is a fraction $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the special fibre $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is a prime element of $B$; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ away from $\varpi_b$, in the sense that $f\in W_0$ iff $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $\varpi_b\nmid h$; the image in $F$ of the $j$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, where `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of $F$ singled out by `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ` (compatibility with the action of `conjElem q γ` on $q$-expansions, normalised by $\zeta\mapsto e^{2\pi i/q}$), the identity if no such automorphism exists; and, finally, the special-fibre identification: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in $\mathrm{Frac}(\,$`CoordRing q κ`$\,)$ of the subgroup generated by the `hFunctionFieldAction` elements attached to $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta'\in C_s$) such that $\#C_s=2\,$`placeWidthChar q M' s` (that is, twice `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`), $\ker\rho$ is generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, $\rho$ agrees on $A_b$ with the $\kappa$-residue map followed by the structure map, every element of the target is a quotient $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$, the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements of the target lying in the image of `CoordRing q κ` inside the Drinfeld function field, and for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f\in B$, the element $\rho($`levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f)$ equals the image of $\rho(f)$ under [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at that element of the subgroup.
--
--   **Rationality of test functions (RAT).** Every $f\in F$ whose underlying Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   **Nodes and the valuative cover.** A finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with the following property: let $V$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ such that, for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ iff the image of $x$ lies in $V$, and such that $V$ is centred over $s$ in the sense that for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, which is regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $j$-element implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base change of $g$), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ in $F$ lies in $F_0$, lies in $V$, and for every $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\kappa$-residue equal to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of that image and $c$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$. Then either every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or there is an $O\in$ `nodes` such that every $f\in O$ lies in $V$ and every non-unit $f$ of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   **The regular prolongation and its ends, stalks and discs.** A field $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$ and a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$, a surjective residue map onto $\mathrm{FSS}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with constants from $A$, with the scaling property), such that for $f\in F_0$ one has $f\in$ `R.integers` iff $f\in W_0$. Further, a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_Q$ of $F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q: A_b[X]\to S_Q$ and $\chi_Q: S_Q\to\kappa$, and sets $D_Q$ of places of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, indexed by the places $Q$, subject to the conjunction: $\#N=q+1$; $Q\notin N$ iff the $R$-residue of every element of $B$ lying in `R.integers` lies in the valuation subring of $Q$; and, for every $Q\notin N$, the following clauses (stated here in summarised form, each being an assertion of the Lean statement): the images in $F$ of the elements of $A_b$ lie in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for $a\in A_b$, with $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ its $\kappa$-residue, and $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(X))=0$; $S_Q$ is local with maximal ideal $\ker\chi_Q$; $S_Q$ is contained in `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀` (image of $K_b$) $\sqcup\,F_0$ and every element of that field is a fraction of elements of $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_Q$ is contained in `R.integers`, and an element of $S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` iff it is divisible by $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$; for $f\in S_Q$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in $Q$'s residue field is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; $B\subseteq S_Q$, and $f\in S_Q$ iff $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ such that the residue at $Q$ of the $R$-residue of $h$ is nonzero; and $P\in D_Q$ iff $P$ is rational, every $f\in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and for every $f\in S_Q$ the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ has $A$-valuation less than $1$ exactly when $\chi_Q(f)=0$. In addition: the discs attached to places outside $N$ are pairwise disjoint (if $P\in D_Q\cap D_{Q'}$ with $Q,Q'\notin N$ then $Q=Q'$); for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_Q$ the order of $P$ at the image of the $j$-expansion is non-negative; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ` leaves $N$ invariant ($\,$`R.resAut τ hτ` $\cdot Q\in N$ iff $Q\in N$) and, for $Q\notin N$, [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (Db Q)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_ResidueDiscs.html#L120) equals $D$ at `R.resAut τ hτ` $\cdot\,Q$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above, for every place $P$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ that is rational and that is centred over $s$ in the following sense — for every $f$ in `R₀.integers` which is regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P'$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P'.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $j$-element implies $0\le P'.\mathrm{ord}(f)$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose $\kappa$-residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$(image of $f$ in $F$) $-\,a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$ — at least one of the two alternatives holds:
--
--   first, there is an $O\in$ `nodes` such that every $f\in O$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and, for every $f\in O$ that is not a unit of $O$, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$;
--
--   or second, there is a place $Q\notin N$ with $P\in D_Q$.
--
--   This is the valuative step in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at the prime $q$: over a fixed supersingular point $s$ of the level-$M'$ special fibre, each rational place of the geometric function field either dominates one of the finitely many node rings of the descended model or lies in the residue disc of a smooth point of the affine chart, the latter being recorded by the stalk data $(S_Q,\varphi_Q,\chi_Q,D_Q)$ indexed by the places outside the set $N$ of $q+1$ ends. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes), where the discs $D_Q$ are converted into residue discs of the semistable covering.
